+
+## 3. Data model
+
+All money integers: **ETB in cents** (`bigint`), **metal in milligrams** (`bigint`). Every table gets `created_at`; nothing money-shaped gets `updated_at` because nothing money-shaped updates.
+
+### 3.1 Ledger core
+
+| Table | Key fields | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `account` | `id`, `owner_type` (user/system), `user_id?`, `asset` (ETB/XAU/XPT), `system_name?` | One row per (owner, asset). System accounts: `system:cash`, `system:vault:XAU`, `system:vault:XPT`, `system:fees`, `system:external` (Chapa in/out), `system:tax`, `system:reforestation` |
+| `ledger_transaction` | `id`, `kind` (deposit/buy/sell/withdrawal/fee/adjustment-treasury), `order_id?`, `payment_id?`, `initiated_by` | Groups entries; the unit of atomicity |
+| `ledger_entry` | `id`, `transaction_id`, `account_id`, `asset`, `amount` (signed bigint) | **Append-only.** DB trigger rejects UPDATE/DELETE. Per transaction, entries must sum to zero per asset — enforced in `LedgerService.post()` and by a deferred constraint trigger |
+
+Balance = `SELECT SUM(amount) FROM ledger_entry WHERE account_id = $1`. A cached `account.balance_cache` may exist for list screens but is never used for spend checks — those recompute under `FOR UPDATE`.
+
+**Concurrency rule (fact-check §2.2):** every posting transaction runs `READ COMMITTED`, first acquiring `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` on all touched `account` rows in a **fixed global order** (by account id) to prevent deadlocks, then checks invariants (sufficient balance, reserve gate, float ceiling), then inserts entries, then commits.
+
+### 3.2 Trading
+
+| Table | Key fields | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `price_tick` | `id`, `asset`, `usd_per_oz_micro`, `etb_rate_micro`, `etb_per_mg`, `source`, `fx_source`, `ts` | Written by worker every ~30s per asset. Source + FX stored for audit (fact-check §7.4) |
+| `quote` | `id`, `user_id`, `side`, `asset`, `grams_mg`, `price_tick_id`, `unit_price_cents_per_g`, `fee_cents`, `tax_cents`, `total_cents`, `expires_at` | **All rounding happens here, once** (fact-check §1.3). Postgres, not Redis. TTL 30s |
+| `order` | `id`, `quote_id`, `user_id`, `status`, `idempotency_key` (unique), `ledger_transaction_id?`, `failure_reason?` | FSM: `created → settled | rejected` (single-step in demo — quote confirm settles atomically or fails with a reason: expired quote, insufficient balance, reserve halt, float halt, tier cap, frozen account) |
+| `fee_schedule` | config-shaped: `commission_pct`, `service_fee_cents`, `tax_pct`, `reforestation_pct` | Loaded from env/config (Decision A1); admin-visible, not admin-editable in demo |
+
+### 3.3 Money in/out
+
+| Table | Key fields | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `payment` | `id`, `user_id`, `chapa_tx_ref` (unique), `amount_cents`, `status` (initiated/webhook_received/verified/credited/failed), `raw_webhook?` | Credit to ledger **only** after server-side `GET /v1/transaction/verify/<tx_ref>` succeeds (fact-check §6.3). Webhook alone never credits |
+| `payout` | `id`, `user_id`, `amount_cents`, `status` (requested/approved/processing/settled/rejected), `approved_by?`, `chapa_transfer_ref?` | Withdrawal: debit user ETB → hold → admin approval → Chapa transfer (or sandbox-mark, fact-check §6.4) |
+
+### 3.4 Treasury & inventory
+
+| Table | Key fields | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `vault_holding` | `id`, `asset`, `grams_mg`, `kind` (intake/outtake), `reference`, `recorded_by` | Physical inventory movements; two-signature in production, single admin + audit log in demo |
+| `treasury_config` | `float_target_cents`, `halt_threshold_cents`, `daily_sellback_ceiling_cents` | Config-driven (Decision A2), demo-labeled values |
+
+Derived, not stored: **reserve ratio** = vault grams vs SUM(user metal accounts); **float** = balance of `system:cash`. Both shown live on the admin treasury panel and the user-facing trust panel.
+
+### 3.5 Identity, compliance, misc
+
+| Table | Notes |
+|---|---|
+| `user` | contact, locale, status (active/frozen), kyc_tier, holding_tier (computed but cached), passkey credentials |
+| `kyc_submission` | doc type (Fayda/passport/licence/kebele), file ref, state (pending/approved/rejected), reviewer |
+| `holding_tier_config` | gemstone tiers: band min/max (ETB cents, USD reference), per-txn cap, daily cap, delivery_eligible (Decision A3) |
+| `compliance_event` | rule key (Q55 set), evidence JSON, action (flag/freeze/review), resolved_by? |
+| `freeze` | user, reason, created_by (rules-engine/admin), lifted_by?, lifted_at? |
+| `audit_log` | append-only: actor, action, target, before/after JSON, ip, ts — every privileged action |
+| `delivery_request` | eligibility snapshot, status (requested/reviewing/approved/scheduled) — request flow only (C6) |
+| `badge`, `user_badge` | activity-only; computed on read (fact-check §3.7) |
+| `ai_conversation`, `ai_message` | chat history, token counts, tool calls made |
+| `notification` | email queue rows (provider send + status) |
