+## 4. The trading spine
+
+```
+price_tick ──► quote ──► order ──► ledger_transaction ──► balances (projection)
+ (30s tick)   (30s TTL,  (idempotent,  (atomic, row-locked,
+  worker)      integers   single-step   invariant-checked)
+               locked)    FSM)
+```
+
+**Buy flow** (sell is the mirror):
+
+1. `POST /quotes {side: buy, asset: XAU, grams_mg | etb_cents}` → quote engine reads latest `price_tick`, computes unit price, commission, tax; **rounds once**; stores quote with `expires_at = now() + 30s`; returns integers + expiry countdown.
+2. `POST /orders {quote_id, idempotency_key}` → single DB transaction:
+   - replay check on `idempotency_key` (return original result if seen)
+   - lock accounts in id order: user ETB, user XAU, `system:cash`, `system:vault:XAU`, `system:fees`
+   - checks: quote unexpired & unused · account unfrozen · user ETB balance ≥ total · **reserve gate**: vault mg − SUM(all user XAU) ≥ quote mg · tier per-txn/daily caps · compliance pre-check (≥ETB 500k → route to review state instead of settling)
+   - post entries: user ETB −total · `system:cash` +total−fee−tax · `system:fees` +fee · `system:tax` +tax · user XAU +mg · `system:vault:XAU` −mg
+   - mark order settled, mark quote consumed, commit.
+3. Failure at any check → order `rejected` with machine-readable reason; nothing posted.
+
+**Sell adds:** float ceiling check (balance of `system:cash` − payout holds ≥ quote total, and daily sell-back ceiling not exceeded) → otherwise order rejects with `float_halt` and the UI explains the published ceiling (C8).
+
