+
+## 5. Payments (Chapa, sandbox)
+
+**Deposit:** `POST /payments` → Chapa `transaction/initialize` (unique `tx_ref`) → redirect to `checkout_url` → user pays (test numbers) → webhook `charge.success` arrives (verify **both** HMAC headers) → server calls `verify/<tx_ref>` → on success, ledger: `system:external` −amount / user ETB +amount → payment `credited`. Return-URL landing polls payment status; it never credits.
+
+**Withdrawal:** `POST /payouts` → ledger moves user ETB → payout-hold sub-account → admin approves in console → Chapa `POST /v1/transfers` (or sandbox-mark if transfers don't run in test mode — pending live-key check, fact-check §6.4) → `payout.success` webhook settles it.
+
+**Channel limits** (fact-check §6.5): deposit UI surfaces per-channel caps (Telebirr 75k, CBEBirr 150k, …) from a config table.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Prices & FX
+
+Worker loop every 30s per asset: fetch gold-api.com → on failure/staleness fetch Swissquote → convert with hourly-cached USD→ETB from open.er-api.com → write `price_tick` (with `source`, `fx_source`). If both sources fail: serve last tick, flag `stale=true`; quote engine refuses to quote on ticks older than 3 minutes (protects against stale-price arbitrage — same reasoning as quote expiry). Chart ranges (24h/7d/30d/1y) read from `price_tick` aggregates; 1y backfilled from seed data for the demo.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Compliance engine
+
+Deterministic rules (Q55 selections), evaluated on order/payment events and login:
+
+| Rule | Action |
+|---|---|
+| Single txn ≥ ETB 500,000 (Q57) | Order → `review` state; human approves/rejects (F21) |
+| Velocity: >N txns in M minutes | Flag → freeze at threshold |
+| Structuring: repeated txns just under 500k | Flag |
+| New device login / many failed logins | Flag; freeze on threshold |
+| Aggregate daily > tier cap | Reject at order time |
+
+Actions write `compliance_event` + optional `freeze` + audit log. **The rules engine freezes; the AI only explains the freeze afterwards** (C2). Unfreeze: compliance role only, never the freezer's own freeze in production (demo: single compliance user, audit-logged). AML export: CSV of flagged events (F22).
+
+---
+
+## 8. AI assistant (Gemini)
+
+- **Model:** `gemini-3.6-flash` (demo), `3.5-flash-lite` (rehearsal) via `@google/genai` in the NestJS `ai` module. No 2.5-series (shutdown 16 Oct 2026).
+- **Tools (read-only, the architectural guarantee):** `get_my_portfolio()`, `get_price(asset, range)`, `get_my_history(limit)`. No write tool exists in the tool list — prompt injection cannot move money because there is nothing to call.
+- **Guardrails:** system prompt = explain, educate, alert; refuse buy/sell recommendations (Decision A4); respond in user's locale (Amharic default). Server-side: tool results are scoped to the authenticated user's id from the JWT — the model never chooses whose data it reads.
+- **Freeze explanation:** when a `freeze` exists, the chat surface injects the freeze reason as context so the assistant explains it in plain Amharic (C2).
+- **Price alerts (F24):** deterministic worker check (e.g. daily move ≥5%) → notification + a non-advisory templated message. The LLM phrases; thresholds trigger.
+
+---
+
+## 9. Identity, roles, admin
+
+- **Auth:** email + password (argon2) with JWT access/refresh; **passkey (WebAuthn) enrollment** post-signup = the "biometric" feature (C3, fact-check §3.4). Account recovery via email.
+- **KYC:** document upload (Fayda/passport/licence/kebele) → review queue → tier assignment. KYC tiers gate deposit/trade activation; holding (gemstone) tiers gate caps + delivery eligibility (Decision A3).
+- **Staff roles (Q47):** `administrator` (config, users, roles — **cannot touch balances**), `compliance` (KYC queue, freezes, AML export), `finance` (treasury panel, payout approvals, reconciliation). Admin console = `/admin` route group in the same Next.js app, role-guarded server-side. Auditor role exists in the model, unused in demo.
+- **No balance-adjust field exists anywhere in the admin UI or API.** Gram supply changes only via settled orders or `vault_holding` treasury operations.
+
