+## 10. Deployment & operations
+
+| Concern | Demo setup |
+|---|---|
+| Environments | `production` only (demo *is* production) + local dev via Docker Compose (Postgres + Redis) |
+| Render services | `web` (paid instance — no cold starts on stage), `api` (paid), `worker` (background worker) |
+| DB | Supabase Postgres; daily automatic backups; migrations run on deploy |
+| Secrets | Render env groups: `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `CHAPA_SECRET_KEY`, `CHAPA_WEBHOOK_HASH`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `FEE_*`, `TREASURY_*`, `TIER_*` |
+| Deploy | Push-to-deploy from GitHub `main`; deployed on Day 1 with a hello-world spine |
+| Monitoring | Render health checks + a `/healthz` endpoint (DB, Redis, price-feed staleness); error alerting via provider email |
+| Seed | Script creating: demo users with history (badges, charts), one frozen account with a compliance trail, vault intake records, treasury config, 1y of backfilled price ticks |
+
+**Third-party dependency list:** Chapa (sandbox keys — created 6 Aug), Gemini (AI Studio key — created 6 Aug), gold-api.com + Swissquote (keyless), open.er-api.com (keyless), email provider (transactional, e.g. Resend free tier), Supabase, Render, domain (client-owned, open item).
+
+**Explicitly not in this design** (spec §5.4): SMS, lending, producer/government dashboards, sentiment analysis, voice, native apps, user-to-user transfers, multi-currency, pen-testing. The permission model accommodates a future regulator read-only role without redesign; it is not built.